; Room objects: 77 records of 11 bytes, the enemies and moving things of each room
;
; Read by the spawner #R$89D9 when a room is entered: it scans the table from the start, calls #R$89ED for every record
; whose room (+0) is the current room and stops at the room byte $1A (the end mark at #R$8EDE, which is also the value
; in $850A, so room and end mark are compared as a word with $8509). The records of one room are not sorted. Record:
; .
; +0 byte: room number
; .
; +1 byte: kind, the index of the handler word in the table at #R$B028 (0-17; the kinds are listed below); the handler
; goes to slot +0 and may change itself while it runs (kind 2 and 3, 4 and 5, 6 and 7 are the two directions of one
; patrol)
; .
; +2 byte: speed, times 4 it becomes the speed word of the slot (+2, 8.8 fixed point, 2-pixel units per frame)
; .
; +3 byte: frames between two animation steps or other timer (slot +$12 counts down, +$13 reloads); for the crusader
; spawner (kind 1) it is the delay before the first crusader, then a new one comes every $28 frames
; .
; +4 byte: x position in 2-pixel units (high byte of the slot's x word at +6/+7)
; .
; +5 byte: y position in 2-pixel units (high byte of the slot's y word at +8/+9)
; .
; +6 byte: initial animation state (slot +$0A and +$0B)
; .
; +7 byte: lower limit of the patrol (slot +4): x for kinds 2 and 3, y for kinds 4-7; low byte of the entity template
; address for kind 1
; .
; +8 byte: upper limit of the patrol (slot +5); high byte of the template address for kind 1
; .
; +9 word: behaviour block (#R$93D3 to #R$95E6) that tells how the kind looks and how large its hit box is
; .
; Kinds (what was seen on the screen after warping to the room): 0 the walkers of the intro in room 0 (Jean and
; crusaders crossing the screen); 1 spawns a running crusader every 40 frames (rooms 5, 6 and 25, where crusaders
; chase Jean in from the left edge); 2 and 3 patrol horizontally (rats, bats, skeletons, soldiers, worms, birds,
; demons: the behaviour block tells which sprite); 4 and 5 patrol vertically (spiders on a thread, flies, fire
; wheels); 6 the hanged men of room 9 (bob on their ropes); 7 is the up-moving state of 6 and 5 the up-moving state of
; 4 (no record starts in state 7); 8 the ghost of room 11 (bounces off tiles); 9 the water drops of rooms 15 and 19;
; 10 skeleton archers; 11 the dragon heads of rooms 20 and 22 that spit bolts; 12 the spore plants of room 14; 13 the
; leaping imps of room 16 (and the river room 19); 14 the head of the Pestilent Beast (its timer runs
; for 110 frames, then flames run along the platform below); 15 the object of room 10 whose handler spawns the
; flame that runs left (#R$BD22); 16 Death of room 18; 17 Satan of room 24.
; .
; Positions are in 2-pixel units (0-127 across, 0-87 down). The lists below give per record: room, kind, creature,
; start x and y, and the patrol limits.
@label=RoomObjects
